  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Thursday)\nIssued at 1102 PM CDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nNear persistence likely through Saturday before the upper ridge\nattempts to weaken slightly as a wave passes across the central\nCONUS on Sunday. The associated weak cold front will likely move\ninto NE OK during the day Sunday and make little to no progress\nthrough Monday. Any post frontal cooling will be minimal and\nlikely offset by moisture pooling along the boundary with the end\nresult being continued high heat index values. Isolated to widely\nscattered storms are possible along and north of the boundary\nhowever widespread meaningful rainfall is unlikely. Ridging aloft\nstrengthens again early next week and the boundary either lifts\nnorthward or becomes diffuse and a return to widespread hot and\ndry weather is expected through mid next week..",
